Data structures are used to store and organize data. Anarrayis an example of a data structure, which 
allows multiple elements to be stored in a single variable.

C++ includes many other data structures as well, each is used to handle data 
in different ways.

These are part of the C++ STL, which stands for TheStandardTemplateLibrary.

STL is a library that consist of differentdata structuresandalgorithmsto effectively store and manipulate data.

If we say that data structures store data, we can say that algorithms are used to solve different problems, 
often by searching through and manipulating those data structures.

Using the right data structure and algorithm makes your program run faster, 
especially when working with lots of data.

